dogma_data: attributions

This package ships small datasets for offline content tests. Each file is listed in DATA_SOURCES.md
with its origin and licence. Attributions:

- Palmer Penguins (penguins.csv): Gorman KB, Williams TD, Fraser WR (2014), PLoS ONE 9(3): e90081.
  Horst AM, Hill AP, Gorman KB (2020), palmerpenguins. Licence CC0 1.0. No attribution is required,
  and the citation is given as a courtesy.
- Synthetic interview-prep files (customers.csv, orders.csv, surveys.csv): generated in this
  repository by sources/interview-prep/generate_mock_data.py. They contain no real people.
- scikit-learn bundled datasets: Pedregosa et al. (2011), JMLR 12, and the scikit-learn BSD-3
  licence for the packaging.
- statsmodels bundled datasets: Seabold S, Perktold J (2010), statsmodels, Python in Science
  Conference. Dataset texts are as recorded in each module's COPYRIGHT string. The spector dataset
  is used with the express permission of its author, who retains all rights.
- Online Retail II (hf/online_retail.csv): Chen D (2019), Online Retail II, UCI Machine Learning
  Repository, doi 10.24432/C5CG6D. Licence CC BY 4.0. The snapshot holds a selection of the
  rows; the source, the pinned revision and the selection are in hf/NOTICE.
- MT-Bench human judgments (hf/mt_bench_judgments.csv): Zheng L et al. (2023), "Judging
  LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena", LMSYS. Licence CC BY 4.0. The snapshot holds a
  selection of the columns; the source and the pinned revision are in hf/NOTICE.
